{title: There is a Fountain}
{artist: William Cowper}
{key: C}

{comment: Verse 1}
[C]There is a fountain [F]filled with [C]blood drawn from Immanuel's [G]veins.
And [C]sinners, plunged [F]beneath that [C]flood, lose all their [G]guilty [C]stains.
Lose all their [G]guilty [F]stains[C], lose all their guilty [G]stains.
And [C]sinners, plunged [F]beneath that [C]flood, lose all their [G]guilty [C]stains.

{comment: Verse 2}
[C]The dying thief [F]rejoiced to [C]see that fountain in his [G]day.
And [C]there may I, though [F]vile as [C]he, wash all my [G]sins [C]away.
Wash all my [G]sins [F]away,[C] wash all my sins [G]away.
And [C]there may I, thought [F]vile as [C]he, wash all my [G]sins [C]away.

{comment: Verse 3}
[C]Dear dying Lamb, Thy [F]precious [C]blood shall never lose its [G]power.
Till [C]all the ransomed [F]Church of [C]God be saved, to [G]sin no [C]more.
Be saved to [G]sin no [F]more[C], be saved to sin no [G]more.
Till [C]all the ransomed [F]Church of [C]God be saved, to [G]sin no [C]more.

{comment: Verse 4}
[C]E'er since, by faith, I [F]saw the [C]stream Thy flowing wounds [G]supply,
[C]Redeeming love has [F]been my [C]theme, and shall be till I [G]die.
And shall be [G]till I [F]die,[C] and shall be till I [G]die.
[C]Redeeming love has [F]been my [C]theme, and shall be till I [G]die.
